# GI-EMISSIVE-LIGHTS (link of GI-ALL-LIGHTS): under the hardware GI tracer the surface cache's direct lighting samples the scene's emissive triangles as lights (the path tracer's one emissive list, picked by power, shadowed by the tracer's ray), and the radiosity leaves the emission of its hits out (counted once). A lamp's glowing shade now lights the wall beside it in the cache, so every GI ray meeting that wall carries the bounce.
# Played by .claude/tools/play_scenario.py <tree> Scenarios/Render/GI-EMISSIVE-LIGHTS.scn, machine.json WITHOUT "HideRayTracing" (an RT device). The baseline is the same file played on a dev tree (origin/dev at this branch's merge-base; copy the file into that tree's Scenarios/Render): every "vs dev" below compares this run's frame with the dev run's frame of the same name, numerically.
# The cases that need another editor launch are sibling files: GI-EMISSIVE-LIGHTS-NORT.scn (case 3, machine.json "HideRayTracing": true), GI-EMISSIVE-LIGHTS-MOVING-NORT.scn (case 4) and GI-EMISSIVE-LIGHTS-MOVING.scn (case 5) - the moving-emitter scene.
# GlobalIllumination.Method is set by the Quality palette's machine override, which REPLACES the scene PPV's request (GI-OVERRIDE-FORCE); the last step puts it back to Level so machine.json is left clean. Reflections.Method stays the level's.
Проект ../BistroFoliageProj/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/B16_Bistro_Street.desce
# Case 0: B16 by day (the sun up at 10:30, the scene's point/spot lights on), the camera above the terrace table looking at the lantern Lantern_Wind_22 (258, 368, 339) and the lit facade behind it.
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position -66,250,570
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.78,0.28,-0.56
Когда run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination.Method HardwareTraced"
Когда frames 120
Тогда-вид 0_day_hwgi [gi_all_lights_link] diff vs dev > 0 in the region around the emissive fixtures (facade/pavement next to the lamp shades and windows), larger there than elsewhere; no NaN/Inf pixel (frame mean finite, no black/white speckle blocks); 0 VUID and 0 "[SceneRenderer] Surface Cache" errors in editor.log
# Case 2: the same scene and camera under the software tracer.
Когда run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination.Method SoftwareTraced"
Когда frames 120
Тогда-вид 2_day_swgi byte-identical to dev up to the GI's own frame-to-frame noise (the software tracer has no emissive list: GI-EMISSIVE-LIGHTS-SW); 0 VUID
# Case 1: GI_Bistro_Night (sun down, lamps and emissive shades only), the camera on the street under the two lamps ahead (MEGALIGHTS-NORT's camera: Streetlight_Glass_01a_6313 left, Lantern_Wind_23 right).
Когда run Scene "Open Scene GI_Bistro_Night.desce"
Когда run View "View mode: Lit"
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position -150,250,300
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction -0.3,0.05,-0.95
Когда run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination.Method HardwareTraced"
Когда frames 120
Тогда-вид 1_night_hwgi walls and pavement beside the emissive shades brighter than dev (mean luminance in the lamp region up), no fireflies above the dev frame's max; 0 VUID
# The night scene under the software tracer with RT shown: case 3's reference (GI-EMISSIVE-LIGHTS-NORT.scn compares its 3_night_swgi_nort with this frame).
Когда run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination.Method SoftwareTraced"
Когда frames 120
Тогда-вид 2_night_swgi the night lamp region under SoftwareTraced, RT shown (the bar 3_night_swgi_nort must match within noise); 0 VUID
Когда run Quality "Quality: GlobalIllumination.Method Level"
Тогда 9_level override removed (machine.json clean of GlobalIllumination.Method)
